{
  "meta": {
    "article_id": "demo-small-experiments",
    "title_en": "Small experiments, clearer thinking",
    "title_zh": "小实验，让思考更清晰",
    "subtitle": "原创短文 · 英语阅读与词汇学习示例",
    "source_type": "article",
    "source_note": "本篇为 Agent 编写的原创演示短文，不是研究论文摘录。示例收藏只用于体验交互。",
    "dictionary_source": "Agent 整理",
    "eyebrow": "THE READING ROOM / 双语精读"
  },
  "pairs": [
    {
      "n": 1,
      "source_id": 1,
      "en": "A small experiment can turn a broad question into something we can observe.",
      "zh": "一个小实验，可以把宽泛的问题变成我们能够观察的事物。",
      "locator": "第 1 段",
      "meanings": {}
    },
    {
      "n": 2,
      "source_id": 2,
      "en": "Before a team begins, it should state its assumption and decide what evidence would challenge it.",
      "zh": "团队开始之前，应当说明自己的假设，并确定什么样的证据会对它构成挑战。",
      "locator": "第 2 段",
      "meanings": {
        "assumption": "假设；未经证实的判断",
        "evidence": "证据"
      }
    },
    {
      "n": 3,
      "source_id": 3,
      "en": "A surprising result is useful when it helps the team revise its explanation.",
      "zh": "出乎意料的结果，只要能帮助团队修正解释，就有价值。",
      "locator": "第 3 段",
      "meanings": {
        "revise": "依据新信息修正"
      }
    },
    {
      "n": 4,
      "source_id": 4,
      "en": "After the experiment, each person can explain the result in their own words.",
      "zh": "实验结束后，每个人都可以用自己的话解释结果。",
      "locator": "第 4 段",
      "meanings": {}
    },
    {
      "n": 5,
      "source_id": 5,
      "en": "Comparing these explanations may reveal a gap that a polished summary would hide.",
      "zh": "比较这些解释，可能会暴露出一份精美总结所掩盖的理解缺口。",
      "locator": "第 5 段",
      "meanings": {
        "reveal": "揭示原先没有看见的情况"
      }
    },
    {
      "n": 6,
      "source_id": 6,
      "en": "The next step is to test the revised idea in a different context and record what changes.",
      "zh": "下一步是在不同情境中检验修正后的想法，并记录发生了哪些变化。",
      "locator": "第 6 段",
      "meanings": {
        "context": "情境；上下文"
      }
    }
  ],
